<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RM_Fluid_Tar_AlphaBiomesAdoption.xml     hand-authored, FLOWWORKS_BUILD_PROGRAM_1 Phase 7
  ============================================================================
  Extends the MayRequire pattern ManyWaters already uses for RM_Slime_* (tint
  AB_SlimeRamp, gated on sarg.alphabiomes, degrade to a working non-AB def
  otherwise) to tar — per row, not globally, per the item's own instruction.

  MECHANISM: RM_Fluid_Tar (Defs/Canals/FluidDefs/FlowWorks_Fluids.xml) and its
  four temporary terrains (Defs/Canals/TerrainDefs/FlowWorks_Terrain.xml) are
  OUR OWN defNames and already resolve without any third-party mod — they ship
  a near-black tint on vanilla's own WaterShallow/ChestDeep/Deep ramps as the
  tinted-vanilla fallback the item requires, so tar never vanishes for a player
  without Alpha Biomes. This patch only reaches into those already-resolvable
  defs and swaps their LOOK when sarg.alphabiomes is active, exactly the "only
  its look degrades" framing of ruling 11 (flowworks_mod_definition.md §16).

  Every Operation is PatchOperationConditional on a real AB def actually being
  loaded (never PatchOperationFindMod on the packageId alone — a stale/renamed
  mod folder could satisfy FindMod while shipping no matching def), so a
  missing or differently-versioned Alpha Biomes prints nothing, per doctrine
  ("a patch that matches nothing logs nothing" is the ACCEPTED failure mode
  here, not a silent bug — the fallback terrain still renders and still
  floods).

  DONOR FACTS, verified directly against Alpha Biomes' own XML on this machine
  (workshop/content/294100/1841354677, packageId sarg.alphabiomes confirmed in
  its own About.xml), NOT against flowworks_mod_definition.md's own citation of
  this donor, which this pass found to be wrong on three of its four names:
    - `AB_Tar` is real: TerrainDef, ParentName="WaterDeepBase",
      texturePath Terrain/Surfaces/AB_TarDeepRamp (1.6/Defs/TerrainDefs/
      Terrain_TarPits.xml). NOT <temporary>true</temporary> (WaterDeepBase
      never sets it), so it cannot be used directly as a FluidDef floodTerrain
      — ConfigErrors would refuse it. That is why this patch retextures OUR
      temporary terrains rather than pointing FluidDef at AB_Tar itself.
    - `AB_TarDeepRamp` is the ONLY tar water-ramp texture AB ships — there is
      no shallow variant. AB's own "tar puddle" (AB_ArtificialTar) reuses the
      same deep ramp at pathCost 200, confirming AB itself does not
      distinguish tar depth by texture either. All four tiers below adopt this
      one texture uniformly, same as the vanilla fallback's one-ramp-per-tier
      convention.
    - `AB_TarPits` (cited in the design doc as an adoptable "surface") is a
      BiomeDef (1.6/Defs/BiomeDefs/Biomes_TarPits.xml), not a paintable
      per-cell terrain. Not adoptable here at all.
    - `AB_TarPuddle` (also cited) is a Plant ThingDef + a Filth texture
      (1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Plants/Plants_TarPits.xml), not a TerrainDef.
    - `AB_TarLakes` (also cited) does not exist anywhere in Alpha Biomes 1.6.
    - `AB_TarMud` ("tarred mud") IS real and IS the natural fit for a receded
      tar lakebed — adopted onto RM_Fluid_Tar.recededTerrain below.
  These three wrong names are a live finding for whoever next edits
  flowworks_mod_definition.md §13; not corrected in that doc by this item
  (out of scope — see the item's own file list), reported as an escalation.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <!-- match-validation: expects exactly 1 hit against /Defs/TerrainDef[defName="AB_Tar"] -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/TerrainDef[defName="AB_Tar"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>/Defs/TerrainDef[defName="RM_Fill_Tar_Trace"]/texturePath</xpath>
      <value>
        <texturePath>Terrain/Surfaces/AB_TarDeepRamp</texturePath>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- match-validation: expects exactly 1 hit against /Defs/TerrainDef[defName="AB_Tar"] -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/TerrainDef[defName="AB_Tar"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>/Defs/TerrainDef[defName="RM_Fill_Tar_Half"]/texturePath</xpath>
      <value>
        <texturePath>Terrain/Surfaces/AB_TarDeepRamp</texturePath>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- match-validation: expects exactly 1 hit against /Defs/TerrainDef[defName="AB_Tar"] -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/TerrainDef[defName="AB_Tar"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>/Defs/TerrainDef[defName="RM_Fill_Tar_Brim"]/texturePath</xpath>
      <value>
        <texturePath>Terrain/Surfaces/AB_TarDeepRamp</texturePath>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- match-validation: expects exactly 1 hit against /Defs/TerrainDef[defName="AB_Tar"] -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/TerrainDef[defName="AB_Tar"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>/Defs/TerrainDef[defName="RM_Fill_Tar_Superdeep"]/texturePath</xpath>
      <value>
        <texturePath>Terrain/Surfaces/AB_TarDeepRamp</texturePath>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- match-validation: expects exactly 1 hit against /Defs/TerrainDef[defName="AB_TarMud"] -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/TerrainDef[defName="AB_TarMud"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>/Defs/RimMandrake.FlowWorks.FluidDef[defName="RM_Fluid_Tar"]/recededTerrain</xpath>
      <value>
        <recededTerrain>AB_TarMud</recededTerrain>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
